{{also|Appendix:Variations of "hon"}}

==English==

===Etymology 1===
Shortened from {{m|en|honey}}.

The transgender slang sense derives from the supposedly abundant use of "hon" as a term of address by older male-to-female transgender people, presumably as a way to verbally affect a femininity they are otherwise perceived by some to lack (due to not [[pass]]ing well), and is especially associated with the cliché phrase "you look great, hon". Derogatory sense likely came about from users of 4chan's /lgbt/ board mocking the discourse on transgender forum Susan's Place.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|hun}}

