====Usage notes====
* Refers to grammatically feminine singular nouns, {{m|cy|hwn||this}} being the masculine singular and {{m|cy|hyn||this}} the (masculine and feminine) plural equivalents.
* In informal language, {{m|cy|hon}} as a determiner is replaced with {{m|cy|yma||there}} used in conjunction with the definite article {{m|cy|y}}, or in some southern dialects with the definite article and {{m|cy|hyn}}.
*: {{lb|cy|formal}} {{uxi|cy|'''y''' ddadl '''hon'''|'''this''' debate}}
*: = {{lb|cy|informal}} {{uxi|cy|'''y''' ddadl ''''ma'''|-}}
*: = {{a|cy|cy-S|informal}} {{uxi|cy|'''y''' ddadl '''hyn'''|-}}
*: {{lb|cy|formal}} {{uxi|cy|'''yr''' eiliad '''hon'''|'''this''' second}}
*: = {{lb|cy|informal}} {{uxi|cy|'''yr''' eiliad ''''ma'''|-}}
*: = {{a|cy|cy-S|informal}} {{uxi|cy|'''yr''' eiliad '''hyn'''|-}}

